  suite_error.pcpp - Test suite: an error test

  kind error: the module is compiled in every cell and must report exactly
  the mistakes its markers name, nothing more. A marker is a line comment
  `// ERROR <code>@<column>: <text>` on the line the report points at: the
  code and the column must match, the text is the start of the message.
  With an ERROR marker the module must not build. Here: one name declared
  twice in one scope.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe suite_error;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

var
  GCount: int32;
  GCount: int32; // ERROR SM0004@3: is already declared in this scope

begin
end.
